    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d759">

                <pb facs="0933" n="845" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg845"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.504/1406</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 311</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-07-01">July 1, 1933</date>.<lb/>[Received July
                        10.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my despatch
                    number 272 dated June 23, 1933, regarding the illegal entry of Chinese nationals
                    into the United States from Mexico and to enclose herewith a copy and
                    translation of note number 11958 dated June 20, 1933, from the Foreign
                        Office<anchor n="63" xml:id="d759-f1"/> in which it is stated that the
                    Ministry of Gobernación has advised that it has issued definitive instructions
                    to the Migration offices on the border to prevent this illegality. This note was
                    received at the Embassy on June 29, 1933.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
